From fa63642182a5d4e7b4d5060f2c5d6274c4555a40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:02:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): chain routed MoE decode kernels with PDL

Upstream base: a75357bba81e31e4f3085700f94b6a0b29aed44a

Rationale: In the routed MoE decode chain (moe_dispatch -> FC1 -> moe_swiglu_cast -> FC2 -> moe_combine), moe_swiglu_cast and early-trigger FC2 already preload routing metadata and weight scales before cudaGridDependencySynchronize(), whereas moe_dispatch and moe_combine waited at kernel entry before doing predecessor-independent work. Move clear_warp_count (zeroing the 26 KB shared-memory expert histogram) before pdl.chain() in moe_dispatch_v41 (part="fused" and part="count") so SMEM initialization overlaps with the upstream router kernel before reading TopkIdx. In moe_combine_v41, preload RoutePos[row, k], Weights[row, k], and Shared[row, bd * block_D + d] into registers before pdl.chain() and unroll the top-k gather loop so routing-table pointer resolution and shared-expert reads overlap with FC2 before waiting on Y.

Quality: Bit-identical across all decode and prefill shapes (torch.equal verified across 208 shape/mode checks and full LayerChain digest checks). Zero stack frame (STACK: 0 across all 28 compiled MoE kernels via cuobjdump --dump-resource-usage).

Tests: pytest -p tests.kernels.deepseek_v41_pdl_sources tests/kernels/moe/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_moe.py tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_pdl.py (151 passed, 0 PDL violations).

Upstream status: Local DeepSeek-V4.1 SM120/SM121 TileLang kernel optimization.
